{
 "name": "R1-02-oracle-void-sets-aside-the-close",
 "note": "cy (founder) names dee as successor; the witness triggers; dee closes cy (counted). Then dee leaves the circle naming counted_to = his acceptance, which puts his later blocks, the close among them, outside his cut. circles.md (The cut) sets aside only a block that speaks for the circle (signed as it, admit/remove, a confirm, an act under a grant to a role, a signal from circle#role). A close is signed under the successor grant, as dee himself. Core: the close still counts, cy is dead, a note cy signs as the circle after it speaks for no one (false). Oracle: circleWhole voids every block of a cut member except answers and removals (fb.cjs:1758-1766 (circleWhole), whose `voided` set is then passed as `exclude` to circleFold, where closedBy reads inScope), so the close is set aside, cy lives again, and the note speaks for the circle (true).",
 "steps": 11,
